/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ Session config via `.qpl.cfg` and the `round` column function.
/
/ Run from the repo root:
/   cargo run -- examples/config_and_round.qpl
/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

trades: load `examples/data/trades.parquet

/ `.qpl.cfg key=value ...` sets session-wide knobs; a bare `.qpl.cfg` prints them
.qpl.cfg maxrow=4 maxcol=6
.qpl.cfg

/ maxrow / maxcol only affect how much is *printed* — the query is unchanged
select from trades

/ `round` is dyadic, q-style: `<precision> round <column>`.
/ precision is an integer literal; the mode comes from `round_type`.
select sym, spread: 2 round price % size from trades

/ HALF_TO_EVEN (banker's rounding) is the default; switch to HALF_UP
.qpl.cfg round_type=HALF_UP
select sym, spread: 2 round price % size from trades
